4.Fixed-Sized Text and Layout Breakage on Zoom
Who is affected
Users with low vision who need to enlarge text to read comfortably re the cluprits for this issue.
The barrier
If font sizes are styled using rigid pixels (px) instead of relative units (rem or em), the text may fail to resize when a user zooms in. Alternatively, if the layout is not responsive, zooming up to 200% might cause sentences to overlap or slide off the edge of the screen without a horizontal scrollbar.
Practical solution
Define all typography using relative scaling units (rem) and build responsive layouts using CSS Flexbox or Grid so the content reflows cleanly when zoomed.

